msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:97
#: c7e307b37d164170833bfdc296da9471
msgid "Tlog's GLOBAL_POSITION relative_alt (altitude above home)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:102
#: ec1ca746e01b4ab4938b2b0660290104
msgid "Changes in the board voltage can also be a sign of a power problem.  Variations of 0.10 to 0.15 volts are normal.  Beyond that could be a sign that other devices sharing the power source with the autopilot are causing ripples in the power supply that could lead to a brown-out.  The board voltage can be graphed using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:104
#: f35457687798423d861a8e23be8ad4ab
msgid "Dataflash POWR message's VCC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:105
#: 115ad9bcf3524ca89c74831067be11b6
msgid "Tlog HWSTATUS's Vcc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:107
#: 365c9fa5a88f4423a461c604a4606e9f
msgid "In the image directly below shows the board voltage sinking by 0.15V when the throttle is raised.  This is generally not a good thing but because it's only 0.15V it's probably OK. The 2nd graph below (a dataflash graph from a different user's log) shows a very stable voltage with ripples less than 0.1V."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:116
#: fb9b880314a544748a1433e8a7f4467b
msgid "Unexpected ERRORS including Failsafes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:118
#: 74bbbfea60484bc7a76f81fabd3d6f1e
msgid "When unexpected behaviour from the autopilot occurs (especially when the user complains that the copter no longer responded to their input) it is often caused by one of the :ref:`failsafes <copter:failsafe-landing-page>` being triggered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:120
#: 9eeaf59be1c244bca4c94e59c8b485df
msgid "The easiest way to find these is to look in the dataflash logs and filter the first column by \"ERR\".  If using the Mission Planner, the errors will also appear in red markers at the top of the graphing area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:125
#: 689321ee85c44a7f827ea8e7d28fcaf2
msgid "The Subsys (aka Sub-system) gives the area that generated the error and the ECode (aka Error Code) tells you what the error was specifically.  The list of subsystems and error codes can be found in the AP_Logger library `AP_Logger.h file <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/AP_Logger.h#L33>`__."
msgstr ""

